# redirects.map — zoth.nealfrazier.tech → studio.nullai.tech

## Purpose
Map every path on the old domain to the same path on the new studio subdomain after Layout B cutover.

## Cloudflare Tunnel / nginx redirect (laptop origin)

Update the `:8088` Cloudflare Tunnel ingress or local nginx so that all traffic for `zoth.nealfrazier.tech` 301-redirects to `studio.nullai.tech`.

### nginx map block (if terminating at local nginx before tunnel)

```nginx
# In the existing zoth.nealfrazier.tech server block (port 8088 or tunnel edge)
map $host $redirect_target {
    default "";
    "zoth.nealfrazier.tech" "https://studio.nullai.tech$request_uri";
}

server {
    listen 80;
    server_name zoth.nealfrazier.tech;

    if ($redirect_target) {
        return 301 $redirect_target;
    }

    # ... existing local :8088 fallback if needed
}
```

### Cloudflare Page Rule (recommended if tunnel-managed)

1. Dashboard → **Rules → Page Rules** → **Create Page Rule**
2. URL pattern: `zoth.nealfrazier.tech/*`
3. Setting: **Forwarding URL (301)** → `https://studio.nullai.tech/$1`

This avoids hitting the laptop origin entirely and offloads the redirect to Cloudflare edge.

## Cloudflare DNS-only alternative (if DNS managed in hPanel)

| Type | Name | Value |
|------|------|-------|
| CNAME | `zoth` | `studio.nullai.tech` |

> Only use this if `zoth.nealfrazier.tech` is already nameservered to Hostinger / hPanel. Do not create a CNAME in hPanel while the domain is still on Cloudflare nameservers, because the Cloudflare proxy will continue serving the old `:8088` content regardless of the hPanel record.

## Per-path examples

| Old URL | New URL |
|---------|---------|
| `https://zoth.nealfrazier.tech/` | `https://studio.nullai.tech/` |
| `https://zoth.nealfrazier.tech/pets/` | `https://studio.nullai.tech/pets/` |
| `https://zoth.nealfrazier.tech/studio/` | `https://studio.nullai.tech/studio/` |
| `https://zoth.nealfrazier.tech/vault/` | `https://studio.nullai.tech/vault/` |
| `https://zoth.nealfrazier.tech/llms.txt` | `https://studio.nullai.tech/llms.txt` |
| `https://zoth.nealfrazier.tech/sitemap.xml` | `https://studio.nullai.tech/sitemap.xml` |

All paths must preserve the full request URI (`$request_uri`). Do not strip query strings or trailing slashes.

## Canonical + link rel updates (after redirect is confirmed live)

Once the redirect is stable, update in-repo canonical URLs so search engines stop indexing `zoth.nealfrazier.tech`:

- `public/index.html` `<link rel="canonical">` + JSON-LD `url`
- `public/studio/index.html` and other `public/studio/*.html` pages
- `public/sitemap.xml` `<loc>` entries
- `public/llms.txt` and `public/agents.md` citations

Do **not** replace across unrelated projects in this disk.
